From b2a712464ea66030c198b0a1e23f5b5ba0e18683 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:02:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: hero name clipping, one continuous chapter stage, Skills
 revealed behind the black hole

Hero name
- word masks padded for the last letter's negative-letter-spacing overhang
  (the cause of the clipped final A/N); fit now also measures glyph overhang
  and height

About chapters (01 -> 03)
- one persistent pinned stage instead of three unpinning visuals; each device is
  a continuous function of the scroll position in chapters (bench-stage.ts), so
  it rises in, settles, and leaves while turning; neighbours' opacities sum to 1
- glass pose now eases toward its target (low-pass of the scroll) and shaders
  are compiled ahead of time when the page is idle

Bridge
- the Skills section is lifted under the stage (SkillsLift); the sheet has a hole
  cut in it by a mask, the hole grows over the real section rising behind it,
  the rim fades past the corners, and the page is simply the Skills section
- tunnel, rings and plates removed; devices still spiral into the hole
